Z||000010||peabody||11-06-1999||09:35 PM||||Sorry, Cooter, a smaller engine wouldn't allow the engine to be moved forward any more than the engine pictured, unless you could find a way to extend the difference between the trans and the ring/ pinion. I think Ryane makes a cradle for a simular set up, but they have the whole drivetrain turned around. That throws the weight ahead of the rear wheels.  ||||reg||9
